---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import ScreenshotCard from "../../components/ScreenshotCard.astro";
import screenshots from "../../data/screenshots.json";
---
<DocsLayout title="Project surfaces — Flynt" description="Flynt project surfaces in 0.12.x.">
  <h1>Project surfaces</h1><p class="lead">Flynt presents one project through multiple surfaces instead of forcing every workflow into a file tree.</p>
  <h2>Project</h2><ul><li><strong>Write:</strong> markdown notes and text artifacts, with git-backed created/modified dates in the note header.</li><li><strong>Lenses:</strong> saved live project queries.</li><li><strong>Graph:</strong> document/task/project relationships. Huge graphs default to a bounded hub overview so the surface stays responsive.</li><li><strong>Omegon:</strong> project-local agent state and runtime artifacts.</li></ul>
  <h2>Tasks</h2><p>Kanban boards and task markdown are indexed into the project store so tasks are navigable project knowledge, not disconnected UI state.</p>
  <h2>Design and visual artifacts</h2><p>Flynt supports Excalidraw drawings, D2 diagrams, design boards, and flow graphs. 0.12.8 bounds wrapper discovery to Flynt artifact folders so large repositories do not pay whole-repo scan costs just to open project surfaces.</p>
  <h2>Terminal</h2><p>Terminal Lab keeps shell sessions inside the workspace. Agent terminal-backed tool calls are surfaced in the ACP panel when attached.</p>
  <h2>Demo vault screenshots</h2><p>These images are controlled by the repository screenshot manifest. Placeholder SVGs keep the site layout stable until the demo-vault screenshot generator replaces them with captured app screenshots.</p><div class="screenshot-grid">{screenshots.map((shot) => <ScreenshotCard {...shot} />)}</div>
</DocsLayout>
